Acknowledgements

No third-party code is vendored here: every kernel, the GGUF reader, the
tokenizer and the engine are written in this repository. What is owed is
intellectual, and named where it was used.

* llama.cpp (MIT, ggml-org/llama.cpp) is the behavioural oracle throughout.
  Every numeric kernel here was checked against values dumped from it with
  `llama-eval-callback`, the tokenizer against `llama-tokenize`, and its source
  was read as the reference for technique — quantization block formats, the
  chat template's shape, and how its CUDA backend quantizes activations. Its
  measured throughput is the baseline this project reports against, including
  where it is ahead.

* pulsar (MIT) for the DeepSeek-V4 port notes and several mechanisms adopted
  from them.

* colibri for the lookahead-recall direction that became this engine's expert
  prefetch.

* The Qwen models (Alibaba) are what this engine was built to run; each model's
  own licence governs its weights, which are not distributed here.
